before:
Put int addBonus(int score); in bonus.hpp. Put the definition in bonus.cpp:
```cpp
#include "bonus.hpp"
int addBonus(int score) { return score + 3; }
```
This ordinary non-inline function has one definition in the program. Its header declaration may be seen by multiple translation units.

Complete local C++ example; the app itself does not execute it:
```cpp
#include <iostream>
#include "bonus.hpp"
int main() {
    std::cout << addBonus(4) << "\n";
}
```

after:
Save each labeled part in the named file, in one folder. Follow the declaration, the definition, and the call as three parts of this one example.

```cpp
// File: bonus.hpp
int addBonus(int score);

// File: bonus.cpp
#include "bonus.hpp"
int addBonus(int score) { return score + 3; }

// File: main.cpp
#include <iostream>
#include "bonus.hpp"
int main() {
    std::cout << addBonus(4) << "\n";
}
```
